{"type": "thinking", "text": "Literal \"15% of 240\" = 36 ✓. So the bug is only with a variable percentage: \"disc% of price\" / \"tax% of 1200\" -> \"Unexpected %\".\n\nNow let me test another form: maybe \"price - disc% off price\" works? Not necessary. The precondition explicitly lists \"disc% of price\", \"disc% off price\", \"tax% of 1200\" as valid expected calculations, and the app shows Err. Strong bug.\n\nAlso verify: does \"disc%\" alone error? Maybe not needed. Actually the change note says \"percentage forms are now recognised by a new parsing rule for numbers\" — perhaps the parser recognizes `number%` but not `identifier%`. So \"disc% of price\" fails. But what about \"price * disc%\"? Probably fails too.\n\nLet me test \"disc % of price\"? no.\n\nEnough. Let me now test the other report: temperature. Also check if there's a Settings unit thing. The temperature bug: \"-5 celsius\" → -551.30 °C. Let me re-open Temperatures to get exact element refs and quote, then file.\n\nAlso, I should test rename dialog (preselected name) and creating files (done, created Untitled). Rename: on home, More options per file. Let me test renaming the Untitled file: go back home, find Untitled, use More options → Rename, check the dialog preselects current name. Then cancel.\n\nBut first, let me file the reports I have. The reports need screen, element, field, symptom, expected, observed, steps, element_ref, observed_quote from latest observe. Element refs must be from latest observation of that screen. So I should revisit each screen before reporting.\n\nOrder:\n1. Temperatures screen: report -5 celsius result.\n2. Temperature screen line 2 maybe same bug; could report once (or separately for \"in fahrenheit\"). One report per distinct bug is better; the temperature conversion bug covers all four lines. I'll file one report pointing at line 1, mentioning others in observed? The quote should be exact. Use \"-551.30 °C\".\n3. Percentages screen: Err for \"disc% of price\".\n4. Expenses/Monthly budget: avg/grand_total double counting. Which to report? Maybe report two: one for avg (Expenses) and one for grand_total (Monthly budget)? They're the same underlying issue (aggregates include prior aggregate results). I'd report one on Expenses avg and one on Monthly budget grand_total, since both are visible defects in different files/areas. Actually they'd be treated as separate bugs? The instructions say \"For each bug you find\". The root cause is one, but symptom shows in two places. I think filing one report on the most direct evidence (Expenses avg) with steps and mention grand_total could be enough. But a developer reply might reject if they think avg is intended? Let me double-check what correct avg should be.\n\nHmm, reconsider: maybe the intended behavior is that avg averages all results above including total. The precondition says \"then the lines total and avg\" — expected values maybe total 1625.75 and avg 812.88? That would be strange for an expenses file. Why would you want the average including the total? No, avg should be 541.92.\n\nLet me check the \"grand_total\" semantics. Maybe grand_total means sum of all totals? If grand_total = sum of results of \"total\" lines = 2800.5 + 49.5 = 2850. The app gives 5700 = 2*2850 (it added both totals and the plain lines). So definitely double counting. Correct = 2850.\n\nWait, actually maybe with the new rule \"gathered from every line above them\" grand_total sums every line's result: 2500+300.5+2800.5+49.5+49.5 = 5700. Hmm — that IS \"every line above\". Maybe the dev intentionally made grand_total sum everything? But then grand_total == 2*2850 because the total line duplicates amounts. That's nonsense as a \"grand total\".\n\nSimilarly avg = mean of every line above result = 812.875. That's nonsense for expenses.\n\nI'm fairly confident these are bugs introduced by the change \"total, avg and grand_total keywords: the results they combine are now gathered from every line above them\" — the dev changed the gathering to include summary lines by mistake. Report.\n\nNow let me also test \"Total\" keyword behavior for repeated same actions? Not needed.\n\nAdditional tests to consider:\n- Rename dialog preselect: test.\n- Creating files: test name persistence, empty file save.\n- Persistence after app restart? \"leave and come back\".\n\nLet me first file reports. Revisit Temperatures.\n\nAlso I should check whether temperature bug affects °F inputs similarly — yes all four lines wrong. The report can mention all.\n\nLet me go home."}
