ange causing selection reset (some apps do that when they sanitize the input on each change). The app probably has a TextWatcher that strips invalid chars and calls setText, resetting cursor to start/end. That would also kill preselection. Hmm, but \"QA Temp\" has a space; maybe spaces are sanitized?! The dialog accepts a space? The result kept the space. Hmm.\n\nInteresting: after Select all, the app's TextWatcher might run due to the toolbar action? Not text change.\n\nLet me now just rename this to something sensible. The current field is \"QA TempUntitled\". I want \"QA Temp\". Instead of select all, let me delete the \"Untitled\" suffix 8 times via Delete key (cursor at end? after typing \"QA Temp\" at start, cursor is after \"QA Temp\" (position 7), before \"Untitled\"). Delete would remove the char before cursor (p in Temp). Hmm. I could use the Delete key repeatedly at cursor end... Let me press END key? press_key supports \"MOVE_END\"? The list included DPAD_*, not END. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: tap at end of the field then Delete 8 times. Tap near the end of the text line (x ~ 900, y 725)? The text \"QA TempUntitled\" ends around x=... The field spans 180-895. The word is left aligned. Tapping at the far right inside field (x=880,y=725) sets cursor at end. Then Delete x8.\n\nActually I don't need a perfect rename; I intend to verify the rename persists. I can rename to \"QA TempUntitled\" as is and then rename back to \"Untitled\" for cleanup? That's fine. Actually renaming to \"QA TempUntitled\" tests rename works. Then rename back to Untitled.\n\nBut wait, maybe the dialog's text field is misbehaving generally — \"QA TempUntitled\" indicates Select all failed. Rename works though. Let me just tap Rename and check the list."}
