the char deletion got reverted by the restoration of the snapshot.\n\nHmm, that's plausible: Undo in this app records line-level snapshots on structural changes and text edits? If text edits aren't stored, undo after editing wouldn't revert them. That could be a bug: \"Undo after editing a value removes an unrelated line\" or \"Undo doesn't restore text edits\".\n\nBut wait, the Undo button was enabled after I deleted the char, could have been enabled from earlier structural changes.\n\nHmm, is this in the scope? The areas are totals/summaries, temperatures/units, percentages, creating/renaming files. Undo behavior is not in those areas, but it relates to \"Reversal: undo, cancel or reverse a change, and check the app returns to the right state.\" It says do test reversal. So an undo bug could be in scope as general QA. But is my observation a genuine bug or did I misread?\n\nActually, let's reconsider: maybe when I tapped Delete key (element 30), because the keyboard was covering the line? No, it deleted one char.\n\nLet's reproduce cleanly: create a new line \"999\" and then Undo. See what happens. Also test: edit a value then Undo → does it revert correctly without removing lines?\n\nActually here's another possibility: my tap on \"Undo\" at (755,148) — the toolbar Undo icon. But maybe the app's undo was \"Redo\"? No, label said Undo.\n\nLet me redo the experiment carefully:\nCurrent state: 100, 200, avg, total. Add line 5 \"abc\"? Let me add \"50\" as line 5, then edit line 2 (change 200→300), then Undo and observe.\n\nThat takes many steps. Alternatively test simpler: current file (4 lines). Tap line 4 or add a line, then Undo. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the observed line-5 disappearance is a real bug but I should verify reproducibility. Let me check Redo: tap Redo — does line 5 come back? If Redo restores line 5, then Undo indeed undid line creation. Let me tap Redo."}
