{"type": "thinking", "text": "Persists after restart. Good.\n\nNow let me check Settings for precision and temperature unit handling. The precondition says \"Result precision is the default of 2 decimals\". Maybe settings has a precision option; not needed.\n\nLet me now revisit the rename preselect with a fresh perspective, since it might be a significant changed feature. Let me try the approach: open rename dialog, wait, then take screenshot and examine precisely at high zoom? The screenshot earlier showed no selection. I've proven with DEL.\n\nCould the dev's \"could not reproduce\" be because they expect the *text to be preselected only for files with names longer than X*? No.\n\nMaybe the app preselects only when the filename contains a dot/extension? All files have no extensions.\n\nMaybe the preselect only happens when you rename via the file's \"More options\" while the file is *locked/pinned*? no.\n\nI could test the \"What's New\" entry for this build to see the wording. Let me check \"What's New\" top entry: it listed 4.9.8 with only Unicode letters. The changed items (temperature, percentage, rename, totals) may be in an \"unreleased\" section? The What's New showed 4.9.8 and 4.9.7. Hmm, the changed-in-this-build list may not be documented.\n\nLet me check Settings for a \"Rename\" related setting? Unlikely.\n\nLet me make a final attempt at the rename bug with a different symptom framing: \"Select all in the rename field does not work / the field's text selection is reset whenever a character is typed\". Maybe the dev can reproduce this. But it's essentially the same. The instructions say a quote that was never on screen gets rejected; quotes are fine. The dev simply says can't reproduce. Maybe the report should be about \"preselection missing\" but the dev's build does have it... Hmm.\n\nActually, wait. Maybe the preselection is implemented and works, but the *dialog opens with the keyboard*, and when the keyboard appears, the IME's \"auto-correct\" selects the word? Our observation contradicts.\n\nLet me try one thing: open rename and check if pressing a *number* key replaces. No difference.\n\nI'll do one more test: open the rename dialog, and without typing, press the \"Done\" key (36) on the keyboard — if text selected, EditText might... no.\n\nAlternatively press \"Cut\" in the floating toolbar. If the whole name is selected, Cut would clear it. But earlier \"Select all\" didn't work. Hmm, but what about long-press then the toolbar has Copy/Cut only if there's a selection? It showed \"Select all\" only initially — that's the standard toolbar when no selection. So definitely no selection.\n\nOK. I'm confident. But since the dev rejected twice, maybe the fix is not present in the build they check? Whatever — I'll accept.\n\nLet me look for other bugs in the four areas that I might have missed:\n\n1. Totals and summaries: grand_total double counting (logged). avg double counting (confirmed). Any other? Test \"prev\" or \"above\"? Not in scope. Maybe \"total\" across blank line (sectioning) - probably intended. Test grand_total when there's only one total? E.g., my test file has line4 total (450 including avg bug). Add grand_total to my test file: grand_total would double count too — same bug.\n\nShould I test the specific changed behavior \"gathered from every line above them\": Suppose a file:\n```\n10\ntotal\n(blank)\n20\ntotal\n```\nDoes the second total include 10? It shows only 20 like Monthly budget. If the change intended \"every line above\" (ignoring blank), the second total should be 30. Hmm! This is a potential second bug: blank-line sectioning prevents \"every line above\". But the precondition explicitly has a blank line in Monthly budget and a second total, which suggests the blank line is intentional to separate groups. If the dev's change intended to gather every line above regardless of blank, the precondition's blank line would be a test of that. Hmm.\n\nWhat does \"results they combine are now gathered from every line above them\" actually mean? Think about the bug they were fixing: previously, maybe total/avg combined only the *immediately preceding contiguous block* of expressions (stopping at blank lines or comments). Now they gather from every line above them. If that's the change, then in Monthly budget, line 6 total should include line 3's total result as well? No — \"results they combine\" may exclude summary lines by design.\n\nHmm, let's think about what a user expects:\n```\nsalary = 2500\nbonus = 300.5\ntotal            → 2800.5\n                 (blank)\ngift = 49.5\ntotal            → ? \ngrand_total      → ?\n```\nIf total gathers every line above, second total = 5650.5 (includes first total) which is absurd because it double counts salary/bonus. Unless total skips summary lines: second total = 49.5. Then grand_total (sum of results of every total line?) = 2850. That's coherent.\n\nThe app currently: second total = 49.5 (consistent with skip-summary + blank?), grand_total = 5700 (includes everything, wrong). The \"every line above\" may refer to *total/avg* behavior across blank lines but skipping summary lines. Hmm.\n\nWhat about Expenses: avg=812.88 means avg did NOT skip the total line. So the new rule \"gathered from every line above\" includes summary lines for avg. Yet the dev confirmed that as a bug. So dev agrees summary lines shouldn't be included in avg.\n\nThen, is the blank line supposed to reset? The dev didn't flag line 6 total=49.5 as wrong. My grand_total report said grand_total is double counting; dev said already logged (same bug). So likely the intended semantics: total/avg sum/average all *expression lines* above in the same section (blank line = section break), excluding summary lines. Then grand_total sums the totals. This matches all preconditions.\n\nSo no additional bug there.\n\n2. Temperatures and units: negative values broken (confirmed). Any other? Positive bare values work; sums work. What about \"-5 celsius in fahrenheit\"? Would be wrong too. Already covered by the sign inversion bug. Also mixed unit sums produce correct results. Good.\n\nTest a negative sum: \"-5 celsius + -10 celsius\" = -15 °C? The sums file has positive. Could test via scratchpad: type \"-5 celsius + -10 celsius\". Parsing may need parentheses. Not necessary; the bug report covers negative single conversions. Hmm, but if the sign inversion is applied to the kelvin base, negative sums may also be broken. E.g., \"-5 celsius + 0 celsius\" = -5 °C. Let me test in the scratchpad since it's quick. Clear and type \"-5 celsius + 0 celsius\". \n\nThe scratchpad currently has \"total\". I need to clear. Select all via long press worked in scratchpad. Let me do that.\n\nActually, wait. The single negative conversion already fails. A negative sum might work or fail, but the confirmed bug covers it. Additional details help the dev but aren't necessary. I'll skip.\n\n3. Percentages: variable percentage forms error (confirmed). Other forms work. Any other? What about \"disc% off price\" - covered. What about percentage results in totals/summary (e.g., \"tax% of 1200\" + total)? The error already breaks it.\n\n4. Creating and renaming files:\n   - Create ✓ (content persists).\n   - Empty creation discarded (probably OK).\n   - Rename works and persists ✓.\n   - Rename preselect ✗ (rejected by dev twice).\n   - Rename cancel preserves old name ✓.\n   - Duplicate names? Untested.\n   - Rename to empty? Untested.\n\nMaybe test renaming an existing file to an existing name. Let me test with my test file: rename \"QA TempUntitled\" → \"Expenses\". If the app allows duplicate, is that a bug? NerdCalci likely appends \"(1)\" or shows an error. Testing could reveal a defect like \"duplicate name allowed causing ambiguity\". It's within \"renaming files\". Let me do it. To clear the field I need to delete 15 characters. Alternatively, I can use the trick: long-press to select all then use the keyboard \"Cut\"?? The toolbar