ther the preselection works for a *new, never-saved* file created via New Calculation: When a new \"Untitled\" file is created, the title is \"Untitled\" and tapping it opens the rename dialog. If the app preselects the current name, the field would show \"Untitled\" selected. Nope, presumably not.\n\nAnother thought: Maybe the preselection only applies when the filename is *different* from \"Untitled\"? No.\n\nI'll try one last variant: open rename dialog and check whether the field's text is selected by using the keyboard's \"Shift+Left\"? There's no shift+arrow. Pressing \"Copy\" in the floating toolbar after long press would copy the whole word if selection... The floating toolbar after long press shows only \"Select all\", meaning long-press didn't select a word either? Normally long-press on a word selects it and shows Copy/Cut/Select all. Here long-press showed only \"Select all\" — that means the long-press did NOT select a word! That's odd: in the scratchpad, long press selected all? Actually in the scratchpad the toolbar showed \"Select all\" only too (element 65) on the first long press, then after tapping Select all, Copy/Cut appeared. So long-press alone showing only \"Select all\" implies the long-press didn't select a word (maybe it positioned the cursor) — normal for some fields? On a standard EditText, long-press selects the word and shows Copy/Cut/Select all. So in both the scratchpad and dialog, long-press didn't select a word. That's an app/field-specific behavior (maybe because the text is a single \"word\" and the app uses a custom input?).\n\nHmm, the scratchpad is the same app's EditText. So the app's text fields might disable text selection handles? That seems unlikely.\n\nOK, at this point I've spent a lot; the rename preselect report stands rejected. I should consider whether there is a different genuine bug I'm missing in the rename area. Let's test renaming to an empty name via a cheaper path: The dialog field can be cleared with 15 DELs