{"type": "text", "text": "The QA sweep is complete. Summary of what I found and tested:\n\n**Confirmed bugs (logged by the developer):**\n1. **Temperature unit conversion** — bare negative temperatures are wildly wrong (`-5 celsius` → `-551.30 °C`, `-10 celsius in fahrenheit` → `-969.34 °F`, etc.), while positive values and temperature sums behave correctly.\n2. **Percentage syntax** — variable-based forms (`disc% of price`, `disc% off price`, `tax% of 1200`) return `Err` / \"Unexpected %\", while literal forms (`10% of 80`, `15% off 240`, `15% of 240`) work.\n3. **Totals/summaries** — `avg` and `grand_total` include already-computed summary lines, causing wrong values (Expenses `avg` = 812.88 vs expected 541.92; Monthly budget `grand_total` = 5,700 vs expected 2,850, which the developer noted was already logged).\n\n**Unresolved concern:** the Rename File dialog's name is prefilled but not preselected (typing appends, Delete removes one character, \"Select all\" ineffective). I reproduced it from both rename entry points, but the developer could not reproduce it twice, so it wasn't logged.\n\n**Verified as working:** totals and averages on ordinary lines, section totals, number bases, date gaps, time differences, remainders, percentage literals, file creation/persistence across restart, rename save/cancel/empty-name validation, deletion, and rotation. Temporary test files were cleaned up, leaving the original nine files intact."}
